### SC-003 — NOT MET (three consecutive clean runs not achieved in this set)
- L2 cross-leaf reachability: genuinely passed in exactly 1 of 3 cycles (cycle 2, 0% loss —
  SC-002 above); cycle 1's apparent pass was a FALSE PASS of the pre-fix grep (it matched
  `100% packet loss`; fix landed on disk after cycle 1 ran) and cycle 3 FAILED
  (`ASSERTION FAILED: no bridged Vlan100 reachability across the overlay … 100% packet loss`)
  (`test-fabric-1.log` line 14, `test-fabric-3.log` line 20; slice
  `gates/proofs/cycles.test-fabric-3.full.slice.txt`).
- L3 intra-VRF / loopback reachability: cycle 3 FAILED —
  `ping6 leaf01(2001:db8:ff::21) -> leaf02(2001:db8:ff::22) … 3 packets transmitted, 0 received,
  100% packet loss` in both directions (`test-fabric-3.log` lines 29–41).
- Inter-VRF isolation (FR-004 spine negatives): VERIFIED in cycle 3 —
  `OK: no VXLAN/VTEP state on spine (CONFIG_DB VXLAN_TUNNEL empty)` and
  `OK: no tenant VRF names detected on spine` on both spines (after one transient
  `Unauthenticated` retry; the refetch+retry landed mid-run, so cycles 1–2 show the pre-retry
  non-answer form).
- Root cause (measured, not speculative): fresh-lab L2/L3 overlay convergence takes 25–37 minutes
  after containerlab deploy (cycle-2 lab: deploy 06:33Z, first passing ping 07:02Z), exceeding
  the suite's bounded wait window; cycle 3's test ran ~20 minutes post-deploy. Fix identified but
  not in this set: a bounded overlay-convergence wait between provision and test in
  `tests/integration/cycles_runner.sh` + `CYCLES_FORCE_RERUN=1` (recorded in PROGRESS.md).
- Status: NOT MET in this run; the suite is fail-closed and the root cause is documented.

