  Root cause: `controllers/srv6service/controller.go` is STATUS-ONLY — `Reconcile` validates the
  compatibility set and patches `Ready`/`Degraded` conditions (with observed generation), but
  never writes an SRv6 SDC Config, so no SRv6 state is ever programmed on the leaves; the
  bootstrap does not program SRv6 either (no SRv6 entries in
  `lab/profiles/sonic-vs/bootstrap/`); the SRv6 suites therefore cannot pass in any live window
  on this code base (`gates/proofs/tests.srv6-capture.log`, `gates/proofs/tests.srv6-failover.log`
  — SKIP-LIVE in the final Absent state).
- WHAT IS VERIFIED: the pinned image's SRv6 capability passes the unchanged gate in 3/3 cycles —
  the gate items `SRv6-Underlay`, `H.Encaps.Red`, `End`, `End.DT46`, `SID-list`,
  `Decapsulation`, `Counters` plus the `sonic-srv6` read-back (item list: `scripts/lib/qualify.sh`
  line 79; execution: `provision-1.log` lines 555, 590–608; slices
  `gates/proofs/scripts.lib.qualify.sh.full.slice.txt`,
  `gates/proofs/cycles.provision-1.qualify-section.slice.txt`). That is image qualification
  (FR-022/T016), not SC-013 service conformance — stated as such, not reclassified.

