## 3. Final checkpoint statement

The checkpoint requires: "All success criteria pass with pinned artifacts, no proprietary
runtime, no silent translation loss, and repeatable cleanup."

Grounded status of each element in this evidence:

- **Pinned artifacts**: PASS — `gates/proofs/verify-pins.run.log` →
  `versions.lock.yaml pins and compatibility are consistent` (`verify-pins rc=0`); supply-chain
  check enforces digest-pinned platform images (`gates/proofs/supply-chain.run.log`).
- **No proprietary runtime**: PASS — enforced SR Linux absence check passes
  (`gates/proofs/supply-chain.run.log`); deny-list visualization boundary passes
  (`gates/proofs/denylist.run.log`); `RUNTIME_SCAN_NO_STANDALONE` final
  (`gates/proofs/cycles/runtime-scan-runtime.log`).
- **No silent translation loss**: PASS — SC-004 VERIFIED (stable renders; unsupported fixtures
  rejected before downstream mutation; `gates/proofs/tests.golden.log`,
  `gates/proofs/tests.unit.log`, `gates/proofs/go-test.all.run.log`).
- **Repeatable cleanup**: PASS — SC-012 VERIFIED (all off runs exit=0 from full AND partial
  states; every no-op repeat exit=0; no owned resources left).
- **All success criteria pass**: NOT MET. In the cited final run set: SC-010, SC-011, SC-012,
  SC-004, SC-005 are VERIFIED; SC-002 is VERIFIED except the Type-5 line accepted as NOT PROVEN
  by the recorded 2026-09-01 operator decision (assertion remains fail-closed); SC-001, SC-007,
  SC-008, SC-014, SC-015, SC-016 are PARTIALLY VERIFIED (the live SDC-data-plane / series-flow /
  value-parity halves are not demonstrated — FINDINGS 1–2); SC-003, SC-006, SC-009, SC-013 are
  NOT MET in this set for the documented root causes in §4. No criterion is claimed beyond what
  the cited logs show; the `test-fabric exit=1` lines in `gates/proofs/cycles/cycles.run.log`
  are the on-disk record of SC-002/SC-003's exact failure sets.

## 4. FINDINGS (root causes of NOT-MET criteria)

1. **SRv6Service device-application layer missing** — `controllers/srv6service/controller.go`
   is status-only (no SRv6 SDC Config write); bootstrap programs no SRv6 device state. Blocks
   SC-013 and the device half of SC-014. The pinned image's SRv6 capability is qualified by the
   gate (3/3 cycles). Fix path: implement SRv6 SDC Config rendering/application in the SRv6
   controller (or provider) + re-run cycles.
2. **In-cluster SDC/kubenet/kuid data plane not running** — `sdc-system`/`kubenet-system`/
   `kuid-system` pods in `ImagePullBackOff` (placeholder digests; `provision-1.log` line 302:
   `0/4 SDC component pods Ready within window`; inventory:
   `gates/proofs/cycles/runtime-inventory-kubectl-3.log`). Upstream image availability for the
   pinned SDC release names was probed and recorded in PROGRESS.md (pass 8 of attempt 1). Blocks
   the SDC-target-readiness half of SC-001 and the SDC target-health half of SC-008.
3. **Fresh-lab overlay convergence exceeds the test window** — L2/L3 convergence measured
   25–37 minutes post-deploy vs ~12-minute suite wait budget; SC-003 passed L2 in 1 of 3 cycles.
   Fix identified (bounded convergence wait in `tests/integration/cycles_runner.sh` +
   `CYCLES_FORCE_RERUN=1`), not included in this set.
4. **Type-5 L3VNI origination image defect** — FRR 10.5.4 in the pinned image does not adopt the
   L3VNI into bgpd's export path (`docs/FABRIC_BGP_EVPN_DEFERRED.md` D-A2, full defect analysis);
   accepted as NOT PROVEN on this image by the recorded operator decision (cited verbatim under
   SC-002).

